# ASI: BrainTokenizer

## Contract

```yaml
module: "brain/master/src/tokenizer/"
trait: "BrainTokenizer"
mandate: "MUST use 'tokenizers = 0.19' crate â€” custom BPE FORBIDDEN"

reason: |
  Qwen2.5 151936-vocab cl100k-like BPE khong the implement correctly
  trong <10KB custom code. tokenizers crate da tested, production-grade.
  3.37KB custom impl -> encode('hello') = ASCII bytes, WRONG.

input_source:
  primary:   "GGUF metadata KV â€” tokenizer.ggml.tokens + tokenizer.ggml.merges"
  fallback:  "tokenizer.json sidecar file (HuggingFace format)"
  load_path: "GgufTokenizer::from_gguf(loaded_model: &LoadedModel)"
```

## Interface

```rust
pub trait BrainTokenizer: Send + Sync {
    // Load vocabulary from GGUF metadata
    fn from_gguf(model: &LoadedModel) -> Result<Self, TokenizerError>
    where Self: Sized;

    // text -> token IDs
    fn encode(&self, text: &str) -> Result<Vec<u32>, TokenizerError>;

    // token IDs -> text
    fn decode(&self, ids: &[u32]) -> Result<String, TokenizerError>;

    fn vocab_size(&self) -> usize;
    fn bos_id(&self) -> Option<u32>;
    fn eos_id(&self) -> Option<u32>;
}
```

## Error contract

```yaml
errors:
  VocabNotLoaded:  "from_gguf() called before load â€” return Err, no panic"
  UnknownToken:    "encode: replace with <unk> id, log warning, no panic"
  Utf8Error:       "decode: lossy utf8, return best-effort string"
  EmptyInput:      "encode('')  -> Ok(vec![]) â€” not an error"
```

## Test expectations (fixtures/hello_tokens.json)

```yaml
model: "Qwen2.5-0.5B"
cases:
  - input:  "hello"
    tokens: [9707]
  - input:  "Hello world"
    tokens: [9707, 1879]   # approximate â€” verify against real model
  - input:  ""
    tokens: []
  - input:  " "
    tokens: [220]

model: "Phi-3-mini"
cases:
  - input:  "hello"
    tokens: [23433]   # verify
```

## GGUF KV keys

```yaml
vocab_key:   "tokenizer.ggml.tokens"    # array<string>
merges_key:  "tokenizer.ggml.merges"    # array<string>
scores_key:  "tokenizer.ggml.scores"    # array<float>
model_key:   "tokenizer.ggml.model"     # string: "gpt2"|"llama"|"rwkv"
bos_key:     "tokenizer.ggml.bos_token_id"
eos_key:     "tokenizer.ggml.eos_token_id"
```

## Cargo dependency

```toml
[dependencies]
tokenizers = { version = "0.19", default-features = false,
               features = ["onig"] }
# onig feature: regex-based pretokenization for cl100k/tiktoken style
```
